<title>GERMANY: German Aug new car registrations up 5.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German Aug new car registrations up 5.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FLENSBURG, Germany 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in Germany rose by 5.3 percent in August from the year-ago month, the Federal Motor Office said on Friday. In the first eight months of 1996, car registrations were up by 7.2 percent against a year earlier.</p>
<p>		     August	  Pct chg/July   Pct chg/Aug 95</p>
<p>    Cars	   228,316	  -25.1		  +5.3</p>
<p>    Trucks	 13,879	   -11.1		  -7.7</p>
<p>    All vehicles 272,898	  -23.5		  +7.0</p>
<p>			     Jan-Aug 1996	Yr/Yr pct change</p>
<p>    Cars		    2,442,715		 +7.2</p>
<p>    Trucks		    128,515		 -9.4</p>
<p>    All vehicles	  2,658,154		 +7.1</p>
<p>The Motor Office also gave the following registration breakdown by manufacturer by German makers and Volkswagen AG foreign subsidiaries.</p>
<p>				Aug 1996</p>
<p>    Volkswagen	    43,165</p>
<p>    Opel/GM		   31,020</p>
<p>    Ford (Germany)	   24,248</p>
<p>    Mercedes	     21,647</p>
<p>    BMW		     13,733</p>
<p>    Audi		   10,844</p>
<p>    SEAT Fiat	     5,085</p>
<p>    Skoda		   1,787</p>
<p>    Porsche		  285</p>
<p>					Jan-Jun 96    Market Share</p>
<p>    Volkswagen		     474,068	     19.4</p>
<p>    Opel/GM			  393,497	     16.1</p>
<p>    Ford			     282,863	     11.6</p>
<p>    Mercedes			 200,021		8.1</p>
<p>    BMW				153,900		6.3</p>
<p>    Audi			     140,636		5.8</p>
<p>    SEAT				36,084		1.5</p>
<p>    Skoda			     14,466		0.6</p>
<p>    Porsche			    4,493		0.2</p>
<p>Note - Opel/GM figure includes Opel Corsa models made in Spain, the GM Pontiac van and GM trucks sold in Europe. The Ford figure includes Fords produced abroad and the Mercedes figure includes Mercedes cars built abroad.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
